o the exact timestamped root.\n  - I verified the merge parents and tree locally with git.\n- **First-root binding:**\n  - `require_first_proof_root` runs before any copy or CLI in `rehearse_import.py` (`main`, right after `bound_candidate`) and in `export_launch_import_proof.py`.\n  - It runs again in `validate_proof` and the freeze path.\n  - I checked locally that it accepts the bound root and refuses the failed 10:52Z root and a one-second-off sibling.\n- **Timing:** `measured_timing_headroom` needs each measured stage (dry, apply, repeat, jobs-OFF readiness and jobs-ON readiness) to be at most 540 s. It also needs at least 600 s left of 5400 s after the stages and 660 s of observation, and the frozen manifest must equal the proof value.\n  - The prior readiness of about 103 s is historical only; the new proof must measure it.\n  - A margin refusal burns this root, so another forward source would be needed.\n- **Guards:** I ran the committed `run_import_guards.py` payload locally (local `python3` instead of the ssh hop) against 630b2354. Result: 175/175 OK, 0 failures/errors/skips, completed 13:44:27 UTC, no production access.\n- **Self-check:** this body passes the 630b2354 `source_review_pass` token check with the actual file hashes.\n\nStill open, and not changed by this pass:\n- The production binding stays UNREVIEWED_NATIVE_FORWARD_REFUSE/0 until a NEW production-source review.\n- The failed f5e root (receipt 511c1951) and the old 5dd build (image 5757) are never reused.\n- Main must stay at 959d17e1, and other application merges stay held until #200 is live and post-checked.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
